@startuml 06-breakdown
!include _style.puml
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #1e293b
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #e2e8f0
  AttributeFontColor #cbd5e1
  StereotypeFontColor #c4b5fd
  HeaderBackgroundColor #334155
}
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #16233b
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #93c5fd
}
title **AS BUILT — Physical Breakdown (ADR-004, ACCEPTED)**\nOption B: one facility table with a kind discriminator. Migration 2026_09_14_090000.

package "Before ADR-004" {
  class "Project" as P0 <<today>>
  class "Subsystem" as S0 <<today>>
  P0 "1" *-- "0..*" S0
  note right of S0
    A flat middle. A project with
    4,000 subsystems had no
    intermediate grouping at all.
    UNIQUE(project_id, code) also
    forced project-wide numbering.
  end note
}

package "Now" {
  class "Project " as P {
    + code : string
    + standards_pack : string
  }

  class Facility <<built>> {
    + id : uuid
    + project_id : uuid
    + code : string
    + name_en / name_fa : string
    --
    + kind : FacilityKind
    ..PLANT | PIPELINE | OFFSITE..
    ..MARINE | UTILITY..
    --
    + addressing : jsonb
    <<validated per kind>>
    --
    + external_ref : string?
    <<Plant 3D PnPID>>
    --
    UNIQUE(project_id, code)
    CHECK kind IN FacilityKind::all()
  }

  class Area <<built, optional level>> {
    + facility_id : uuid
    + code : string
    + unit_code : string?
    --
    <<= Plant 3D "Area">>
    <<= AWP "CWA">>
    --
    UNIQUE(facility_id, code)
  }

  class "Subsystem " as SS <<migrated>> {
    + facility_id : uuid  <<NOT NULL>>
    + area_id : uuid?  <<nullable>>
    + code, discipline
    --
    UNIQUE(facility_id, code)
    ..was UNIQUE(project_id, code)..
    --
    + fullCode()
    + blocksMechanicalCompletion()
    + closurePercent()
  }

  class FacilityKind <<value object>> {
    + all() : drives the CHECK
    + selectable() : excludes PIPELINE
    + requiresStationing() : bool
    + label(en|fa) : string
    + areaLabel(en|fa) : string
  }

  P "1" *-- "0..*" Facility
  Facility "1" *-- "0..*" Area
  Area "0..1" <-- "0..*" SS : optional
  note on link
    **subsystems_area_within_facility**
    FK (area_id, facility_id)
     -> areas (id, facility_id)
    ON DELETE SET NULL

    A composite FK, not two separate
    ones: it makes "area belongs to a
    different facility" unrepresentable
    rather than merely discouraged.
  end note
  Facility "1" <-- "0..*" SS : always
  Facility ..> FacilityKind

}

package "Untouched — subsystem_id in 6 tables" {
  class PunchItem
  class McCertificate
  class MaterialLot
  class PurchaseOrderItem
  class MaterialMovement
}

SS "1" <-- "0..*" PunchItem
SS "1" <-- "0..1" McCertificate
SS "1" <-- "0..*" MaterialLot
SS "1" <-- "0..*" PurchaseOrderItem
SS "1" <-- "0..*" MaterialMovement

note bottom of Facility
  **Why one table and not plants + pipelines.**
  A plant is bounded by coordinates; a pipeline by
  stationing (KP 0+000 .. KP 147+500). Two sibling
  tables would force every upward query into a
  two-branch COALESCE and an XOR CHECK constraint -
  the classic smell of a missing abstraction.

  What they genuinely share is being a *commissioning
  parent*. What differs is *spatial addressing*, which
  is exactly what a per-kind jsonb column is for.

  Same pattern this codebase already proved twice:
  McCertificate.state, and MovementType instead of
  four document tables.
end note

note bottom of Area
  **Optional on purpose — and the fixture proves it.**
  PL-01/AR-22 -> SS-2201 · PL-01/AR-33 -> SS-3301
  PL-01/(none) -> SS-5501  <- optional area on a
  facility that DOES use areas
  PL-02 has no areas at all -> SS-4401, SS-6601
  ---
  Plant 3D's own refinery example has 13 areas, so
  skipping the level would break lossless import.
  But an Iranian booster station with 12 subsystems
  should not have to invent 12 areas.

  Absence of structure must not be reported as an
  error - same rule as closurePercent() returning
  100 for an empty punch list.
end note

note right of FacilityKind
  Plant 3D has **no** System/Subsystem, no MC,
  no punch, no handover - it is a design
  authoring tool. Compatibility therefore means
  a documented **import mapping**, not a copied
  schema:

  Area property -> areas.code
  Unit subpart  -> areas.unit_code
  PnPID         -> external_ref
end note

@enduml
